From e4111693ed7222e03271232751c6d5e5fff54f83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 19:45:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Security audit follow-up: socket auth, mass-assignment
 allowlists, timing-safe webhook check, HTML-escaping, businessOnly wiring

- backend/middlewares/socketAuth.js (new): Socket.io connections previously
  joined `business_<id>` rooms purely on client say-so
  (socket.on('join_business', businessId) => socket.join(...)), with no
  authentication at all. Any socket could join any tenant's room and
  silently receive that business's live customer conversations
  (customer phone numbers, names, full message text). socketAuth()
  verifies the same JWT used for REST auth during the handshake and
  resolves the caller's OWN business id server-side; server.js now uses
  io.use(socketAuth()) and auto-joins only that resolved room. The
  client-controlled join_business event is removed entirely.
  frontend/src/hooks/useSocket.js sends the JWT on connect.

- backend/controllers/businessController.js: updateProduct/updateAppointment
  scoped the findOneAndUpdate FILTER to the caller's own business but
  passed req.body straight through as the UPDATE document. `business`
  is a real, writable field on both schemas, so a tenant could PATCH a
  record it owns with { business: '<victim-id>' } and reassign it onto a
  different tenant - e.g. planting an attacker-controlled product into a
  competitor's catalog, which then feeds into that business's AI system
  prompt. Added pickAllowed() field-allowlisting (same pattern already
  used by updateBusiness), runValidators: true, and proper 404s.

- backend/controllers/conversationController.js: updateStatus hardened the
  same way (allowlisted field, runValidators, 404, null-safe business
  lookup).

- backend/services/paystackService.js: webhook signature check now uses
  crypto.timingSafeEqual instead of a plain === comparison, matching the
  pattern already used for the Meta webhook signature.

- backend/controllers/adminController.js: escape regex metacharacters in
  admin business-search before using them in a  filter (ReDoS fix).

- backend/controllers/authController.js: changePassword now enforces the
  same 8-char + complexity policy as register/resetPassword instead of a
  weaker, inconsistent 6-char rule.

- backend/utils/htmlEscape.js (new), used from emailService.js and
  cronService.js: user-supplied free text (account owner name, business
  name) was interpolated unescaped into HTML email bodies.

- backend/routes/index.js: wired up the previously-unused businessOnly
  middleware across all tenant-scoped routes so an account with no
  business gets a clean 403 instead of a 500.

- Added backend/tests/{socketAuth,massAssignment,htmlEscape}.test.js
  (83 -> 99 passing tests).
